  <prompt>Replace PlaceholderTrapVerifier's T6 branch with a real check combining KV secret presence (the cert) AND a Graph containerType GET performed under ClientCertificateCredential (app-only proof) -- proving the confidential-client auth model is actually in effect, not merely configured.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in H13's IE2ETrapVerifier/IE2EInvariantVerifier seam contracts and typed Azure SDK/REST post-condition verification.</role>

  <goal>T6's real verifier confirms the SPE cert secret is present in KV AND that a live Graph containerType GET succeeds under ClientCertificateCredential, returning Fail if either check fails.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §6: 'T6 SPE confidential-client creation... KV secret presence + Graph containerType GET under ClientCertificateCredential (app-only proof)... Blocked by: H8 real + 24h gate elapsed.' The 24h SPE replication gate is an EXTERNAL, session-free wait this probe must tolerate (WaitingOnGate is a legitimate outcome, not a failure) until it has genuinely elapsed.</background>
